# Cursor Rules for {{ cookiecutter.project_name }}

You are working on a TypeScript library that uses pnpm, Biome, TypeScript and Vitest.

## Commands

- Install: `pnpm install`
- Lint and format: `pnpm format`
- Type check: `pnpm typecheck`
- Test: `pnpm test`
- Build: `pnpm build`
- Full gate: `make check && make test`
{% if cookiecutter.agent_profile == "full" %}
## Code Style

- ES modules; relative imports end in `.js`
- Strict TypeScript, no `any`; `import type` for type-only imports
- 120 character lines, double quotes, semicolons (Biome enforces these)
- TSDoc on every export

## Testing

- Tests in `tests/*.test.ts`, importing from `../src/*.js`
- Write a failing test before fixing a bug
- Cover error paths
{% endif %}
## PR Guidelines

- Small, focused PRs
- Include/update tests
{%- if cookiecutter.changelog %}
- Add an entry under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md` for user-facing changes, using the Keep a Changelog categories (Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, Security)
{%- if cookiecutter.agent_profile == "full" %}; create the category heading if missing, e.g. `### Fixed` then `- Reject an empty name in greet.`{% endif %}
{%- endif %}
- Conventional Commits: feat:, fix:, docs:, refactor:, test:, chore:
